{
  "source": "course-assets/probability-and-prediction/probability-and-prediction.mp4",
  "duration": 161.408,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 6.72,
      "text": "When you type a prompt into ChatGPT and receive a coherent response, it can feel like the system is thinking."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.42,
      "end": 14.74,
      "text": "Tools like Claude appear to understand context and nuance, leading us to wonder what is actually happening behind the interface."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.62,
      "end": 21.92,
      "text": "These systems function by calculating probability, analyzing the statistical likelihood of what should happen next."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.92,
      "end": 28.76,
      "text": "This process of predicting outcomes based on specific data traces back to 1654, when"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.76,
      "end": 33.54,
      "text": "mathematicians Blaise Pascal and Pierre de Fermat exchanged letters about the odds"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.54,
      "end": 34.16,
      "text": "in gambling."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.88,
      "end": 38.56,
      "text": "Their work provided the foundation for how we calculate the chance of a future"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.56,
      "end": 42.88,
      "text": "event, a framework that remains central to how modern AI builds an answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.6,
      "end": 47.7,
      "text": "To see how that works, we start with standard probability."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.7,
      "end": 52.7,
      "text": "This applies to scenarios where every possible outcome is equally likely. The"
    },
    {
      "start": 52.7,
      "end": 56.52,
      "text": "math is a simple division. You count the ways to get the specific result you"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.52,
      "end": 61.82,
      "text": "want and divide that by the total number of possible outcomes. Consider a"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.82,
      "end": 67.3,
      "text": "basic scenario. You toss two coins. To find the chance both land on heads, we"
    },
    {
      "start": 67.3,
      "end": 72.54,
      "text": "map out the possibilities. There are four equally likely results. Only one"
    },
    {
      "start": 72.54,
      "end": 76.8,
      "text": "matches our goal. We divide that successful path by the four total"
    },
    {
      "start": 76.8,
      "end": 84.88,
      "text": "outcomes, giving a probability of 25%. However, odds are rarely static. In mathematics, conditional"
    },
    {
      "start": 84.88,
      "end": 90.38,
      "text": "probability describes how new evidence changes the calculation. Imagine we run the toss"
    },
    {
      "start": 90.38,
      "end": 95.32,
      "text": "again, but this time someone peaks. They tell you the first coin landed on heads."
    },
    {
      "start": 95.94,
      "end": 100.78,
      "text": "Because the first coin is heads, we can immediately eliminate any outcome starting"
    },
    {
      "start": 100.78,
      "end": 106.16,
      "text": "with tails. Those possibilities are ruled out. Our total pool of outcomes has shrunk"
    },
    {
      "start": 106.16,
      "end": 113.12,
      "text": "from 4 to 2. Out of those two remaining paths, only 1 results in double heads. 1 divided"
    },
    {
      "start": 113.12,
      "end": 118.68,
      "text": "by 2 means the probability jumps to 50%. The physical state of the coins didn't"
    },
    {
      "start": 118.68,
      "end": 123.96,
      "text": "change, but your knowledge of them did. AI uses conditional probability to answer"
    },
    {
      "start": 123.96,
      "end": 129.34,
      "text": "your questions. If you ask, what should I name my new dog, and the AI begins its"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.34,
      "end": 134.56,
      "text": "response with, you could name him, those words become the context for the next calculation."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.56,
      "end": 141.6,
      "text": "It might find a 22% chance for Spot, 17% for Max, and 14% for Buddy."
    },
    {
      "start": 143.04,
      "end": 145.52,
      "text": "Once a word is chosen, it is added to the text."
    },
    {
      "start": 145.98,
      "end": 151.96,
      "text": "This updated string of words becomes the new evidence for the next calculation, and the cycle repeats instantly."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.58,
      "end": 157.64,
      "text": "AI builds answers with probabilities, one prediction at a time."
    }
  ],
